  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect would set your life total to a specific number that's higher than your current life total, that effect would cause you to gain life equal to the difference. Boon Reflection will then double the amount of life that effect would cause you to gain. For example, if you have 3 life and an effect says that your life total “becomes 10,” your life total will actually become 17.",
      "oracle_id": "b86d3142-568a-4eea-b1ae-5fcfc1453533",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In a Two-Headed Giant game, only Boon Reflection's controller is affected by it. If that player's teammate gains life, Boon Reflection will have no effect, even when that life gain is applied to the shared team life total.",
      "oracle_id": "b86d3142-568a-4eea-b1ae-5fcfc1453533",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The effects of multiple Boon Reflections are cumulative. For example, if you control two Boon Reflections, you'll gain four times the original amount of life. If you control three Boon Reflections, you'll gain eight times the original amount, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "b86d3142-568a-4eea-b1ae-5fcfc1453533",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If your life total becomes 0 or less, you'll lose the game before you can activate the ability of Children of Korlis.",
      "oracle_id": "d44a8f89-b9c0-4e8a-9179-baa0c448a3c9",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The life you gain is based on the total amount of life you lost, not the difference in your life total from when the turn started. For example, if you lose 5 life and gain 3 life before activating the ability, the ability will cause you to gain 5 life, not 2.",
      "oracle_id": "d44a8f89-b9c0-4e8a-9179-baa0c448a3c9",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any enters-the-battlefield abilities of the chosen permanent will trigger when Clever Impersonator enters the battlefield. Any \"as [this permanent] enters the battlefield\" or \"[this permanent] enters the battlefield with\" abilities of the chosen permanent will also work.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clever Impersonator copies exactly what is printed on the chosen permanent (unless that permanent is copying something else or is a token; see below). It doesn't copy whether that permanent is tapped or untapped, whether that permanent has any counters on it or any Auras and/or Equipment attached to it, and it doesn't copy any non-copy effects that have changed that permanent's power, toughness, types, color, abilities, or so on.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Clever Impersonator enters the battlefield as a copy of a planeswalker, it will enter the battlefield with a number of loyalty counters on it equal to the loyalty printed in the lower right corner of the planeswalker card. It won't copy the number of loyalty counters on the original planeswalker.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Clever Impersonator enters the battlefield at the same time as another permanent, it can't become a copy of that permanent. You may choose only a nonland permanent that's already on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the chosen permanent has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the chosen permanent is a copy of something else (for example, if the chosen permanent is another Clever Impersonator), then your Clever Impersonator enters the battlefield as whatever the chosen permanent copied.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the chosen permanent is a token, Clever Impersonator copies the original characteristics of that token as defined by the effect that put that token onto the battlefield. Clever Impersonator is not a token.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Remember that if you control more than one legendary permanent with the same name, you'll choose one to remain on the battlefield and put the rest into their owner's graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can choose not to copy anything. In that case, Clever Impersonator enters the battlefield as a 0/0 creature, and it's put into the graveyard immediately (unless something is raising its toughness above 0).",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose which nonland permanent Clever Impersonator will copy, if any, as it enters the battlefield. This doesn't target that nonland permanent.",
      "oracle_id": "d4ec0df9-a4a3-48cf-a0aa-b1aea5c49142",
      "published_at": "2014-09-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you lose enough life to lower your life total to 0 or less, you’ll lose the game as a state-based actions before you activate Tainted Sigil’s ability.",
      "oracle_id": "f39fd4bd-3157-42da-9a39-94e094b5f681",
      "published_at": "2009-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tainted Sigil’s ability checks only whether life was lost. It doesn’t care whether life was also gained. For example, say one player lost 4 life during the turn and no one else lost any, but that same player also gained 6 life that turn. That player has a higher life total than they started the turn with — but Tainted Sigil’s ability counts only the life loss, so you’ll gain 4 life.",
      "oracle_id": "f39fd4bd-3157-42da-9a39-94e094b5f681",
      "published_at": "2009-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tainted Sigil’s ability counts the life lost by all players, including you.",
      "oracle_id": "f39fd4bd-3157-42da-9a39-94e094b5f681",
      "published_at": "2009-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When Tainted Sigil’s ability resolves, it checks how much life each player lost over the course of the turn, then it totals that number and you gain that much life in one shot. It doesn’t matter how a player lost life or what caused it. It also doesn’t matter if Tainted Sigil wasn’t on the battlefield when some or all of the life was lost.",
      "oracle_id": "f39fd4bd-3157-42da-9a39-94e094b5f681",
      "published_at": "2009-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
